sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: lemma
----
proof:

Let {ABC|ABCh} be a right-angled triangle having the angle {A|angA} right, and let the perpendicular {AD} be drawn.

I say that the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {BA}, the rectangle {BC} by {CD} equals the square on {CA}, the rectangle {BD} by {DC} equals the square on {AD}, and the rectangle {BC} by {AD} equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC}, and first that the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {BA}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.33 Lemma diagram" src="propX33lemma.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's lemma figure: the right triangle ABC (A on the circle on BC,
    // which Joyce names ABC) with the perpendicular AD, drawn as the two
    // random-faced triangles ABD and ACD. Added, all hidden at rest: solid
    // twins AB, AC, BC, AD (initiallyHidden) so the triangle stands before
    // the perpendicular and AD strokes from A; transparent targets BD, DC
    // (;0;0;0); faceless, strokeless triangle twins ABCh / ABDh / ADCh that
    // carry the highlights (#140), reached with the display override
    // ({ABC|ABCh} — the circle owns the name ABC); right-angle markers at A
    // (by hypothesis) and at D (the perpendicular).
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): B, C (free) and A (circle
    // slider), all givens. D is a derived foot and listed from "let the
    // perpendicular AD be drawn".
    var L_TRI  = ["A","B","C","AB","AC","BC","angA"];
    var L_PERP = L_TRI.concat(["D","AD","BD","DC","angD"]);
    var L_ALL  = L_PERP.concat(["ABD","ACD"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.33",
        elements: [
            "B;point;free;30,170",
            "C;point;free;250,170",
            "M;point;midpoint;B,C;0;0",
            "ABC;circle;radius;M,B;0;0;0;0",
            "A;point;circleSlider;ABC,120,40",
            "D;point;foot;A,B,C",
            "ABD;polygon;triangle;A,B,D;0;0;black;random",
            "ACD;polygon;triangle;A,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide-only twins, highlight targets and markers.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D;0;0;0",
            "DC;line;connect;D,C;0;0;0",
            "ABCh;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ABDh;polygon;triangle;A,B,D;0;0;0;0",
            "ADCh;polygon;triangle;A,D,C;0;0;0;0",
            "angA;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,B,C",
            "angD;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,A,B"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","AC","BC","AD"],
        aliases: { "CB": "BC", "BA": "AB", "CA": "AC", "CD": "DC", "DA": "AD" },
        slides: [
            { text: "Let {ABC|ABCh} be a right-angled triangle having the angle {A|angA} right,",
              visible: L_TRI,
              highlighted: ["ABCh","angA"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "Lemma" }] },
            { text: "and let the perpendicular {AD} be drawn.",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["AD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AD",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "I say that the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {BA},",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["BC","BD","AB"] },
            { text: "the rectangle {BC} by {CD} equals the square on {CA},",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC","AC"] },
            { text: "the rectangle {BD} by {DC} equals the square on {AD},",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["BD","DC","AD"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {BC} by {AD} equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC},",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["BC","AD","AB","AC"] },
            { text: "and first that the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {BA}.",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["BC","BD","AB"] },
            { text: "Since in a right-angled triangle {AD} has been drawn from the right angle perpendicular to the base,",
              visible: L_PERP,
              highlighted: ["AD","angA","angD","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore the triangles {ABD|ABDh} and {ADC|ADCh} are similar both to the whole {ABC|ABCh} and to one another.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABDh","ADCh","ABCh"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "ACD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "ABD, ADC similar to ABC", ref: "VI.8" }] },
            { text: "Since the triangle {ABC|ABCh} is similar to the triangle {ABD|ABDh},",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCh","ABDh"] },
            { text: "therefore {CB} is to {BA} as {BA} is to {BD}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","AB","BD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CB : BA = BA : BD", ref: "VI.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {AB}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","BD","AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CB·BD = AB²", ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason the rectangle {BC} by {CD} also equals the square on {AC}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC","AC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC·CD = AC²", ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "Since, if in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular is drawn from the right angle to the base,",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","angA","angD"] },
            { text: "then the perpendicular so drawn is a mean proportional between the segments of the base,",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","BD","DC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "the perpendicular is a mean proportional", ref: "VI.8.Cor" }] },
            { text: "therefore {BD} is to {DA} as {AD} is to {DC}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AD","DC"] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {BD} by {DC} equals the square on {AD}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","DC","AD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BD·DC = AD²", ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "I say that the rectangle {BC} by {AD} also equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","AD","AB","AC"] },
            { text: "Since we said, {ABC|ABCh} is similar to {ABD|ABDh}, therefore {BC} is to {CA} as {BA} is to {AD}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABCh","ABDh","BC","AC","AB","AD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC : CA = BA : AD", ref: "VI.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {BC} by {AD} equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC}.",
              visible: L_ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","AD","AB","AC"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "Lemma") return "#lemma";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification
    // (shared by both canvases on this page).
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VI.4":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI4/",
        "VI.8":     "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI8/",
        "VI.8.Cor": "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI8/#cor",
        "VI.17":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI17/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since in a right-angled triangle {AD} has been drawn from the right angle perpendicular to the base, therefore the triangles {ABD|ABDh} and {ADC|ADCh} are similar both to the whole {ABC|ABCh} and to one another. [!just VI.8]

Since the triangle {ABC|ABCh} is similar to the triangle {ABD|ABDh}, therefore {CB} is to {BA} as {BA} is to {BD}. Therefore the rectangle {CB} by {BD} equals the square on {AB}. For the same reason the rectangle {BC} by {CD} also equals the square on {AC}. [!just VI.4; VI.17]

Since, if in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular is drawn from the right angle to the base, then the perpendicular so drawn is a mean proportional between the segments of the base, therefore {BD} is to {DA} as {AD} is to {DC}. Therefore the rectangle {BD} by {DC} equals the square on {AD}. [!just VI.8.Cor; VI.17]

I say that the rectangle {BC} by {AD} also equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC}.

Since we said, {ABC|ABCh} is similar to {ABD|ABDh}, therefore {BC} is to {CA} as {BA} is to {AD}. [!just VI.4]

Therefore the rectangle {BC} by {AD} equals the rectangle {BA} by {AC}.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find two straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them rational but the rectangle contained by them medial.
----
proof:

Set out two rational straight lines {AB:canvas_1} and {BC:canvas_1} commensurable in square only such that the square on the greater {AB:canvas_1} is greater than the square on the less {BC:canvas_1} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB:canvas_1}. [!just X.30]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="330" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.33 diagram" src="propX33.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: AB with BC produced beyond B, D bisecting BC, E on AB,
    // the semicircle AFB (random face), the triangle AFB (random face, named
    // ABB) and the perpendicular EF. Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins
    // AB, AF, FB (initiallyHidden) so AB stands before the semicircle and
    // the joins stroke from A and F; transparent targets AE, EB, BD, DC
    // (;0;0;0); a faceless, strokeless twin of the semicircle (semiT) to
    // carry its highlight, since the filled one would be raised over the
    // triangle (#140) and the circle that owns the name AFB is the whole
    // circle; the right angle at E. ABEF is Joyce's slip for the rectangle
    // AB by EF and is left literal.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B (free), C (line slider)
    // — the givens — and E (line slider), which only arrives with "let it be
    // the rectangle AE by EB", so it is deferred. D and F are derived and
    // listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","AB","BC"];
    var BIS   = GIVEN.concat(["D","BD","DC"]);
    var APPL  = BIS.concat(["E","AE","EB"]);
    var SEMI  = APPL.concat(["semi"]);
    var PERP  = SEMI.concat(["F","EF","angE"]);
    var ALL   = PERP.concat(["AF","FB","ABB"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_1",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.33",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;40,160",
            "B;point;free;200,160",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A,B,290,160",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "M;point;midpoint;A,B;0;0",
            "AFB;circle;radius;M,B;0;0;0;0",
            "D;point;midpoint;B,C",
            "E;point;lineSlider;A,B,170,160",
            "EF';line;perpendicular;E,A;0;0;0",
            "FF';line;chord;EF',AFB;0;0;0",
            "F;point;last;FF'",
            "semi;sector;arc;B,F,A;0;0;black;random",
            "ABB;polygon;triangle;A,B,F;0;0;black;random",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            // Slide-only twins, highlight targets and markers.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "AF;line;connect;A,F",
            "FB;line;connect;F,B",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E;0;0;0",
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D;0;0;0",
            "DC;line;connect;D,C;0;0;0",
            "semiT;sector;arc;B,F,A;0;0;0;0",
            "angE;sector;angleMarkerRight;E,A,F"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","AF","FB"],
        deferDraggables: ["E"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "BE": "EB", "BF": "FB", "FE": "EF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To find two straight lines incommensurable in square",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.33" }] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on them rational but the rectangle contained by them medial.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "Set out two rational straight lines {AB} and {BC} commensurable in square only",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "such that the square on the greater {AB} is greater than the square on the less {BC}",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB, BC as required", ref: "X.30" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {BC} at {D}.",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["BC","D"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "D", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Apply to {AB} a parallelogram equal to the square on either of the straight lines {BD} or {DC}",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["AB","BD","DC"] },
            { text: "and deficient by a square figure, and let it be the rectangle {AE} by {EB}.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "E", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE·EB = BD²", ref: "VI.28" }] },
            { text: "Describe the semicircle {AFB|semiT} on {AB},",
              visible: SEMI,
              highlighted: ["semiT","AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "semi", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "draw {EF} at right angles to {AB},",
              visible: PERP,
              highlighted: ["EF","angE"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "EF",   name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and join {AF} and {FB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AF",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "FB",  name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "ABB", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Since {AB} and {BC} are unequal straight lines,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "and the square on {AB} is greater than the square on {BC}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "while there was applied to {AB} a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "that is, to the square on half of it, and deficient by a square figure, making the rectangle {AE} by {EB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BD","AE","EB"] },
            { text: "therefore {AE} is incommensurable with {EB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE, EB incommensurable", ref: "X.18" }] },
            { text: "And {AE} is to {EB} as the rectangle {BA} by {AE} is to the rectangle {AB} by {BE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB","AB"] },
            { text: "while the rectangle {BA} by {AE} equals the square on {AF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","AE","AF"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {AB} by {BE} is to the square on {BF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","EB","FB"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AF} is incommensurable with the square on {FB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "Therefore {AF} and {FB} are incommensurable in square.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "Since {AB} is rational, therefore the square on {AB} is also rational,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "so that the sum of the squares on {AF} and {FB} is also rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AF² + FB² = AB²", ref: "I.47" }] },
            { text: "Since, again, the rectangle {AE} by {EB} equals the square on {EF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB","EF"] },
            { text: "and, by hypothesis, the rectangle {AE} by {EB} also equals the square on {BD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EB","BD"] },
            { text: "therefore {FE} equals {BD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EF","BD"] },
            { text: "Therefore {BC} is double {FE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","EF"] },
            { text: "so that the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also commensurable with the rectangle ABEF.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC","EF"] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is medial,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {AB} by {EF} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB·BC medial", ref: "X.21" },
                               { claim: "commensurable with a medial area", ref: "X.23.Cor" }] },
            { text: "But the rectangle {AB} by {EF} equals the rectangle {AF} by {FB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","EF","AF","FB"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {AF} by {FB} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB·EF = AF·FB", ref: "Lemma" }] },
            { text: "But it was also proved that the sum of the squares on these straight lines is rational.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "Therefore two straight lines {AF} and {FB} incommensurable in square have been found",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on them rational, but the rectangle contained by them medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AF","FB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.33") return "#prop";
            if (ref === "Lemma") return "#lemma";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.47":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI47/",
        "VI.28":    "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI28/",
        "X.18":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX18/",
        "X.21":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX21/",
        "X.23.Cor": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX23/#cor",
        "X.30":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX30/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Bisect {BC} at {D}. Apply to {AB} a parallelogram equal to the square on either of the straight lines {BD} or {DC} and deficient by a square figure, and let it be the rectangle {AE} by {EB}. [!just VI.28]

Describe the semicircle {AFB|semiT} on {AB}, draw {EF} at right angles to {AB}, and join {AF} and {FB}.

Since {AB} and {BC} are unequal straight lines, and the square on {AB} is greater than the square on {BC} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {AB}, while there was applied to {AB} a parallelogram equal to the fourth part of the square on {BC}, that is, to the square on half of it, and deficient by a square figure, making the rectangle {AE} by {EB}, therefore {AE} is incommensurable with {EB}. [!just X.18]

And {AE} is to {EB} as the rectangle {BA} by {AE} is to the rectangle {AB} by {BE}, while the rectangle {BA} by {AE} equals the square on {AF}, and the rectangle {AB} by {BE} is to the square on {BF}, therefore the square on {AF} is incommensurable with the square on {FB}. Therefore {AF} and {FB} are incommensurable in square.

Since {AB} is rational, therefore the square on {AB} is also rational, so that the sum of the squares on {AF} and {FB} is also rational. [!just I.47]

Since, again, the rectangle {AE} by {EB} equals the square on {EF}, and, by hypothesis, the rectangle {AE} by {EB} also equals the square on {BD}, therefore {FE} equals {BD}. Therefore {BC} is double {FE}, so that the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is also commensurable with the rectangle *ABEF.*

But the rectangle {AB} by {BC} is medial,
therefore the rectangle {AB} by {EF} is also medial. [!just X.21, X.23.Cor]

But the rectangle {AB} by {EF} equals the rectangle {AF} by {FB}, therefore the rectangle {AF} by {FB} is also medial. <div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX33/#lemma">Lemma</a></div>

But it was also proved that the sum of the squares on these straight lines is rational.

Therefore two straight lines {AF} and {FB} incommensurable in square have been found which make the sum of the squares on them rational, but the rectangle contained by them medial.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

The first part of the lemma encompasses proposition @I.47, but the proof of it depends on the theory of similar triangles developed in Book VI, unlike Euclid's proof of I.47.

This proposition is used in propositions @X.39 and @X.76.
----
red_highlight: yes
